```json
{
  "summary": "Added `stuckReported` flag to prevent duplicate warnings when a task is stuck. The watchdog now only logs/emits TASK_STUCK event once per stuck task instead of on every check cycle.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "Watchdog/Periodic Task Patterns",
      "reminder": "When implementing periodic health checks, always guard against duplicate notifications using a 'reported' flag - otherwise you'll flood logs every check interval"
    },
    {
      "topic": "State Management",
      "reminder": "In-memory state flags like `stuckReported` are lost on service restart. Consider if database sync is needed for critical state"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Task Lifecycle",
      "reminder": "Always reset state flags (stuckReported, isKilled, killCount) when untracking or re-tracking a task to avoid stale state issues"
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "location": "lines 196-205",
      "description": "Task is still killed on every check cycle after first stuck report - only the warning is suppressed, but killTask() is called unconditionally. This could cause excessive kill attempts.",
      "detail": "The logic at line 202 runs every cycle regardless of stuckReported status. After maxKillsPerTask is reached, the task is marked as stuck, but until then kill attempts happen repeatedly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "location": "lines 157-165",
      "description": "stuckReported flag is never reset when task is untracked. If same taskId is re-tracked later, it will have stale state.",
      "detail": "The untrackTask method doesn't reset any state - this is fine for killCount/isKilled since they persist in DB, but stuckReported being true could suppress future warnings."
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "priority": "high",
      "description": "Consider adding a delay or backoff between kill attempts, or only attempt kill once per stuck detection cycle (not every check interval)"
    },
    {
      "priority": "medium",
      "description": "Add test coverage for the stuckReported flag behavior - verify warning is emitted exactly once per stuck task"
    },
    {
      "priority": "low",
      "description": "Document the stuckReported behavior in the interface or add JSDoc explaining when it resets"
    }
  ],
  "praise": [
    "Clean implementation - adding just one field solves the duplicate log spam issue",
    "Good use of early continue to skip already-marked-as-stuck tasks",
    "Proper use of !== vs ! for clarity in the guard condition"
  ],
  "overallScore": 75,
  "codeQualityScore": 80,
  "testCoverageScore": 60,
  "documentationScore": 65
}
```

